  "description": "3. Flux 2 Klein 9B KV FP8 - 3 Images Edit is a general utilities workflow designed to demonstrate a focused reusable ComfyUI utility using FLUX.2 Klein 9B. Its 26-node graph exposes 1 prompt/text field(s), 3 media input target(s), and 1 save/preview stage(s), while preserving the original editor-format graph for reference. The ComfyUI editor graph was converted to API format and is ready for live validation against the connected node and model registry.",
  "category": "Utilities & Workflow Tools",
  "subcategory": "General utilities",
  "episode": "EP09",
  "instructions": "1. Open the workflow and select Validate. SineForge will compare every node class and input against the currently connected ComfyUI instance without queueing it.\n2. Review the model-file entries in Requirements and place each checkpoint, text encoder, VAE, LoRA, or auxiliary model in the folder documented by the source workflow. Refresh ComfyUI after adding files.\n3. Upload and assign the required image, mask, video, or audio files to the listed media inputs. Keep the source dimensions and duration appropriate for the selected model.\n4. Edit the positive/negative prompt, resolution, sampler, steps, guidance, and seed. Use a fixed seed while tuning composition, then vary it deliberately.\n5. Save a copy before making structural changes. Use Editable inputs for normal parameters and Raw API JSON only when you need to inspect or change graph wiring.\n6. Validate again after every change. Queue one workflow only after validation passes; then inspect the returned output, logs, duration, dimensions, and media integrity.",
